<title>JAPAN: NCB shares surge on tie-up news.</title>
<headline>NCB shares surge on tie-up news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Credit Bank Ltd rose sharply in Thursday afternoon trade after the bank announced it had agreed a business tie-up with Bankers Trust New York Corp.</p>
<p>As of 0545 GMT, the shares were 33 yen or 19.64 percent higher at 201, with trade totalling 19.82 million shares. It was the largest percentage gainer as well as the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
<p>The shares had been bid-only throughout the morning session and for most of the afternoon session.</p>
</text>
